      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Solway began as a small railway village in 1887, growing during a logging boom that saw the Solway Lumber Company process billions of board feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/solway_minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in Solway in 1898, and the historic 1899 Solway Mercantile Store still houses JD’s Outpost bar and grill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solway%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlers in Solway were Swedish, Norwegian, and Danish immigrants who arrived in 1899, bringing a mix of Northern European cultures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/solway_minnesota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2022, the Beltrami County Historical Society partnered with local media to highlight Solway’s heritage, preserving its logging legacy.",
